00:04:06.746 --> 00:04:08.147
The boys, though, honey,
they're very sick.

00:04:08.147 --> 00:04:09.381
We should go.
It's diarrhea."

00:04:09.381 --> 00:04:12.852
"No one is going anywhere!

00:04:12.852 --> 00:04:19.258
Oh, Cyrus, when will you put
a lock on the gun room door?"

00:04:19.258 --> 00:04:23.028
And lastly, let's dispense
with this ridiculous lie

00:04:23.028 --> 00:04:25.064
that has become canon
on the right

00:04:25.064 --> 00:04:29.301
that standing up to any
sensible gun safety legislation

00:04:29.301 --> 00:04:31.904
means standing up for
the Second Amendment.

00:04:31.904 --> 00:04:33.773
It's one of the greatest cons
in the history of politics.

00:04:33.773 --> 00:04:35.307
For most of American history,

00:04:35.307 --> 00:04:36.743
the idea that
the Second Amendment

00:04:36.743 --> 00:04:39.445
guarantees an individual right
to own whatever gun you want

00:04:39.445 --> 00:04:40.947
was never even contemplated.

00:04:40.947 --> 00:04:43.316
Conservative Supreme Court
Justice Warren Burger

00:04:43.316 --> 00:04:44.717
famously called it a fraud.

00:04:44.717 --> 00:04:47.253
-If I were writing
the Bill of Rights now,

00:04:47.253 --> 00:04:50.323
there wouldn't be any such thing
as the Second Amendment.

00:04:50.323 --> 00:04:51.490
-Which says?

00:04:51.490 --> 00:04:54.426
-That a well-regulated militia

00:04:54.426 --> 00:04:56.963
being necessary for the defense
of the state,

00:04:56.963 --> 00:04:58.897
people's right to bear arms.

00:04:58.897 --> 00:05:01.400
This has been the subject
of one of the greatest pieces

00:05:01.400 --> 00:05:04.370
of fraud --
I repeat the word fraud --

00:05:04.370 --> 00:05:08.107
on the American public
by special interest groups

00:05:08.107 --> 00:05:10.443
that I have ever seen
in my lifetime.

00:05:10.443 --> 00:05:12.445
Now, just look at those words.

00:05:12.445 --> 00:05:14.680
There are only three lines
to that amendment.

00:05:14.680 --> 00:05:17.149
"A well-regulated militia."

00:05:17.149 --> 00:05:20.386
If the militia, which was
going to be the state army,

00:05:20.386 --> 00:05:22.555
was gonna be well-regulated,

00:05:22.555 --> 00:05:27.093
why shouldn't 16 and 17 and 18
or any other age persons

00:05:27.093 --> 00:05:29.428
be regulated in the use of arms?

00:05:29.428 --> 00:05:31.196
-That point
is so blindingly obvious,

00:05:31.196 --> 00:05:32.931
it's shocking
we even have to debate it.

00:05:32.931 --> 00:05:34.166
When the amendment was written,

00:05:34.166 --> 00:05:37.269
even the militia was supposed to
be well-regulated.

00:05:37.269 --> 00:05:39.538
Do you think the founders
would look at this and say,

00:05:39.538 --> 00:05:41.707
"That's exactly what we meant"?

00:05:41.707 --> 00:05:44.176
And that's not even taking
into account that the founders

00:05:44.176 --> 00:05:47.046
could never have conceived
of the weapons we have now.

00:05:47.046 --> 00:05:49.115
In their day, it took
nine minutes to load a gun,

00:05:49.115 --> 00:05:50.916
and half the time,
you pulled the trigger,

00:05:50.916 --> 00:05:54.120
and it just went "ppfff" and
the shot fell out on your shoe.

00:05:54.120 --> 00:05:56.622
Those dorks
were tying keys to kites

00:05:56.622 --> 00:05:58.424
to learn about electricity.

00:05:58.424 --> 00:06:01.393
If you let Ben Franklin
fire an AR-15,

00:06:01.393 --> 00:06:04.830
he would [bleep]
his burlap yoga pants.

00:06:04.830 --> 00:06:08.101
"Deborah, I invented
electricity!"

00:06:08.101 --> 00:06:11.204
"Invent some better pants, Ben!"

00:06:13.105 --> 00:06:16.142
[Bleep] hilarious, but his wife
was named Deborah.

00:06:18.010 --> 00:06:22.615
I would have thought the first
Deborah was born in like 1940.

00:06:24.850 --> 00:06:28.220
Or how about private sales
of guns, like at gun shows,

00:06:28.220 --> 00:06:30.656
which often don't even require
background checks,

00:06:30.656 --> 00:06:33.726
a loophole the vast majority
of Americans want closed?

00:06:33.726 --> 00:06:35.528
Watch this clip and ask yourself

00:06:35.528 --> 00:06:37.497
whether the people who wrote
the Second Amendment

00:06:37.497 --> 00:06:39.331
would consider this
well-regulated.

00:06:39.331 --> 00:06:40.699
-If you buy a gun from someone

00:06:40.699 --> 00:06:42.601
in the business
of dealing in firearms,

00:06:42.601 --> 00:06:45.037
federal law
requires background checks.

00:06:45.037 --> 00:06:47.706
But the private dealers
are not legally required

00:06:47.706 --> 00:06:49.208
to conduct background checks.

00:06:49.208 --> 00:06:51.810
-I would ask you for
a Virginia driver's license.

00:06:51.810 --> 00:06:54.113
That way I know you're
from within the state.

00:06:54.113 --> 00:06:56.248
-But if I gave you a fake
Virginia driver's license,

00:06:56.248 --> 00:06:57.850
you would never know?
-I would have no idea.

00:06:57.850 --> 00:06:59.485
-Would you trust me?
Do I have an honest face?

00:06:59.485 --> 00:07:01.420
Would you sell it to me?
-I'd trust you.

00:07:01.420 --> 00:07:04.056
Think you have an honest face.
-Okay, but that being said,

00:07:04.056 --> 00:07:05.625
sometimes if you don't think
someone has an honest face,

00:07:05.625 --> 00:07:07.026
if you have a bad vibe,
you don't sell it?

00:07:07.026 --> 00:07:08.527
-Correct.
-That's right.

00:07:08.527 --> 00:07:11.230
All you need to buy a gun in
this country is an honest face.

00:07:11.230 --> 00:07:14.566
We better hope to God Paul Rudd
never decides to raise an army

00:07:14.566 --> 00:07:16.035
and overthrow
the U.S. government.

00:07:16.035 --> 00:07:19.872
By the way, that dude's almost
two years older than Ted Cruz.

00:07:19.872 --> 00:07:21.840
That's what happens when
you moisturize your face

00:07:21.840 --> 00:07:23.309
instead of your hair.

00:07:23.309 --> 00:07:26.645
Paul Rudd would have to spend
seven hours in a makeup chair

00:07:26.645 --> 00:07:30.282
to look like a man
20 months his junior.

00:07:30.282 --> 00:07:31.484
The idea that
the Second Amendment

00:07:31.484 --> 00:07:33.519
guarantees an individual right
to own a gun

00:07:33.519 --> 00:07:35.721
unconnected with service
in a militia,

00:07:35.721 --> 00:07:37.890
an idea that was codified
in 2008

00:07:37.890 --> 00:07:40.493
by the conservative majority in
the disastrous Heller decision,

00:07:40.493 --> 00:07:43.396
is, to borrow Warren Burger's
phrasing, a fraud.

00:07:43.396 --> 00:07:46.532
In fact, the argument
is so absurd that in 1982,

00:07:46.532 --> 00:07:48.267
Senate Republicans
issued a report

00:07:48.267 --> 00:07:49.869
claiming to have discovered...

00:07:58.544 --> 00:08:00.679
I'm sorry, long-lost proof?

00:08:00.679 --> 00:08:04.016
Was it written in invisible ink
on the back of the Constitution?

00:08:04.016 --> 00:08:06.451
Or did you discover
a secret stone tablet

00:08:06.451 --> 00:08:07.653
